T Generated span
# The two piers were written by hand. Everything between them was generated:
#   node cli.js bridge builds/demo_bridge.knx LT RT --style arch --rod blue --rod blue --segments 6 --append
# Try the other techniques on the same two points: --style truss, line, slide.
# The pier tops lie in the xz plane, which is the plane the arch springs in. A connector is a plane, and
# an arch can only land on one that contains it.
! two piers
C LA W8 -4,0,0.5 y x
C LT W8 -4,0,4.5 y x
R LA LT
C RA W8 4,0,0.5 y x
C RT W8 4,0,4.5 y x
R RA RT
A LA
A RA

! bridge LT to RT, arch
C BR1 W8 -3.3908,0,6.405
C BR2 W8 -1.9367,0,7.7781
C BR3 W8 0,0,8.2773
C BR4 W8 1.9367,0,7.7781
C BR5 W8 3.3908,0,6.405
R LT BR1 blue beam
R BR1 BR2 blue beam
R BR2 BR3 blue beam
R BR3 BR4 blue beam
R BR4 BR5 blue beam
R BR5 RT blue beam
